Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for your interest in Arizona State University. The RN to BSN program provides associate degree and diploma-trained nurses an opportunity to complete their BSN.

The program is delivered entirely online, which allows nurses to continue working in their profession while completing their bachelor’s degrees. With five start dates per year and classes running every 7.5 weeks, students can expect to complete their BSNs in as little as 15 to 18 months. The curriculum for this program, including all lower-division prerequisites and co-requisites and upper-division core courses, can be viewed online at https://asuonline.asu.edu/rnbsn/degree-program/curriculum. To begin the RN to BSN program, you will first need to apply to ASU (https://webapp4.asu.edu/uga_admissionsapp/?program=UGNU&plan=NUNURDBSN&subplan=&favoritescore=0&campus=ONLNE).

If you have any additional questions, please call 866-277-6589 or request more information through ASU Online (https://asuonline.asu.edu/rnbsn#asuo-rfi-form).

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}


If you would like any additional information or have questions related to this subject, please reply to this email.

